    <DataNode elementId="AT5G04490-MONOMER" textLabel="AT5G04490-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LZ76" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; mutant &lt;i&gt;vte5-1&lt;/i&gt; generate by ethylmethane sulfonate (EMS) mutagenesis was shown to be affected in tocopherol biosynthesis in the seeds of the mutant plants |CITS:[16361393]|. This mutant was additionally shown to have elevated amounts of phytol. The &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis VTE5&lt;/i&gt; gene was heterologously expressed in &lt;i&gt;E. coli&lt;/i&gt;. Extracts of the transgenic bacterium converted phytol into its monophosphorylated form (phytolmonophosphate, PMP) only; no phytyl pyrophosphate was detected after addition of phytol to the extract, showing that the enzyme encoded by &lt;i&gt;VTE5&lt;/i&gt; is a phytol kinase. The enzyme exhibits highest activity in the presence of CTP as cosubstrate, while ATP and GTP do not support the phytol kinase reaction |CITS:[16361393]|. Phytol kinase activity was detected in protein extracts of &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; leaves, more specifically in the chloroplast envelope membrane |CITS:[16306049]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G04490-MONOMER" />
